t⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x+15\\pi ) & =cot⁡(-x+\\pi \\cdot 15) \\\\  & =cot⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x) & =-cot⁡x \\\\  & =-(-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}cot⁡(-x+15\\pi )+7 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6+7 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}+7 \\\\  & =3+7 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158064/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "43754cfc-c3dd-515d-ba83-cd68897b2d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "7d5bbc22-46ca-5577-b870-6c69749bd7ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "232b36d0-235e-581c-ad5f-a1ce7c1001f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "1efa56ad-5cac-581d-87f5-daf6e5b8e8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "cd74a48e-9f91-55d3-88f9-ddf0f38ff5b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db81b4bc-5a86-5f30-8343-97b7fbfaf2e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-136559/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-136559/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-136559/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-136559/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-136559/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-136559/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-136559" :question/id #uuid "39378440-a829-50ce-ab74-9b393b345cdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-136559" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\frac{1}{4},$ then $4cot⁡(-x+4\\pi )+1=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x+4\\pi ) & =cot⁡(-x+\\pi \\cdot 4) \\\\  & =cot⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x) & =-cot⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4cot⁡(-x+4\\pi )+1 & =4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})+1 \\\\  & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-136559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698"] :knowledge-point/